Subject: [PATCH] soc: rockchip: sip: add the PX30 DDR frequency IDs

Rockchip's downstream BL31 for PX30/RK3326 changes the DDR rate through
ROCKCHIP_SIP_DRAM_FREQ like the RK3399 one, but the request travels in
pages shared with the firmware: x1 names the page type, x3 the command.
Add the IDs a PX30 DMC driver needs on top of the RK3399 ones: the DDR
interface version query (same number as SET_ODT_PD, different meaning
on this firmware), the share-memory request, the DDR page type and the
"switch still pending" return of SET_RATE.

Values from rockchip-linux/kernel (develop-5.10)
include/linux/rockchip/rockchip_sip.h and
include/soc/rockchip/rockchip_sip.h.
---
--- a/include/soc/rockchip/rockchip_sip.h
+++ b/include/soc/rockchip/rockchip_sip.h
@@ -17,4 +17,16 @@
 #define ROCKCHIP_SIP_CONFIG_DRAM_SET_PARAM	0x07
 #define ROCKCHIP_SIP_CONFIG_DRAM_SET_ODT_PD	0x08
 
+/*
+ * Rockchip's downstream BL31 for PX30/RK3326 and later SoCs reuses
+ * ROCKCHIP_SIP_DRAM_FREQ with a different calling convention: the rate goes
+ * through pages shared with the firmware, x1 names the page type and x3 the
+ * command. ROUND_RATE, SET_RATE and GET_RATE keep the numbers above.
+ */
+#define ROCKCHIP_SIP_CONFIG_DRAM_GET_VERSION	0x08
+#define ROCKCHIP_SIP_SHARE_MEM			0x82000009
+#define ROCKCHIP_SIP_SHARE_PAGE_TYPE_DDR	2
+/* SET_RATE returned before the switch; BL31 raises the complete IRQ */
+#define ROCKCHIP_SIP_RET_SET_RATE_TIMEOUT	-6
+
 #endif
